    <bpmn:process id="W_W3809" name="W3809. Trade-Capability Strategy &amp; Apprenticeship Program Charter" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual people strategy (links to VS-33.1/VS-103.3); capability gap
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Enterprise trade-capability strategy
Owner: Trade Capability / L&amp;D / Store Ops
Participants: Trade Capability, L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4), Store Ops (links to VS-07), In-Store Services (links to VS-09), Installation (links to VS-12), HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), Workforce Planning (links to VS-103.3), Strategy (links to VS-33)
Source: workflow W3809 — Trade-Capability Strategy &amp; Apprenticeship Program Charter</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3809_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3809_Lane1" name="Trade Capability">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3809_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3809_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3809_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3809_Lane2" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3809_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3809_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3809_Start4" name="Annual people strategy (links to VS-33.1/VS-103.3); capability gap">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3809_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3809_Task5" name="Trade Capability/L&amp;D/Store-Ops define the trade-capability strategy: identify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trade Capability/L&amp;D/Store-Ops define the trade-capability strategy: identify the critical trade roles and skills BuildRight must master (lumber/yard, tiles/flooring, plumbing, electrical, paint/tinting, hand/power tools, hardware/fasteners; plus fabrication/estimation/installation), assess current capability gaps, and set the target capability posture and build-vs-buy approach
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / L&amp;D / Store Ops
Accountable (A): CHRO / COO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3809_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3809_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3809_Task6" name="Trade Capability/L&amp;D charter the apprenticeship program as the primary…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trade Capability/L&amp;D charter the apprenticeship program as the primary capability-build vehicle: program objectives (certified trade capability, succession for trade-master roles, scalable service quality), target cohorts/scale, the TESDA-registered model (links to W3811), and the link to workforce planning (links to VS-103.3) and store growth (links to VS-37)
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / L&amp;D / HR
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3809_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3809_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3809_Task7" name="CHRO/Executive ratify the trade-capability strategy and apprenticeship charter…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CHRO/Executive ratify the trade-capability strategy and apprenticeship charter, approve the program budget (links to W3812), and cascade to category/store leadership as a BuildRight capability priority
Responsible (R): CHRO / Trade Capability
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3809_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3809_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3809_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3809_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-598 (ensure controlled execution — Apprenticeship Program Design, TESDA Registration &amp; Governance (PA-123.1).) | - operational: capability strategy; operational: formal charter
Owner: Trade Capability / L&amp;D / Store Ops</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
