    <bpmn:process id="W_W3810" name="W3810. Apprenticeship Curriculum &amp; Competency Standard Design" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Charter (W3809); curriculum cycle
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Trade-apprenticeship curriculum per trade
Owner: Trade Capability / L&amp;D
Participants: Trade Capability, L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4), Master Tradespersons (links to VS-07/VS-09), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Quality (links to VS-31), Compliance (links to VS-22), Vendor/Product experts
Source: workflow W3810 — Apprenticeship Curriculum &amp; Competency Standard Design</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3810_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3810_Lane1" name="Trade Capability">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3810_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3810_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3810_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3810_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3810_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3810_Start3" name="Charter (W3809); curriculum cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3810_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3810_Task4" name="Trade Capability/L&amp;D design the apprenticeship curriculum and competency…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trade Capability/L&amp;D design the apprenticeship curriculum and competency standard per trade: theory modules, practical competencies (e.g., lumber grading/board-foot, tile laying/grout, pipe fitting, basic electrical safety, paint tinting/colour matching, power-tool operation/safety), mapped to TESDA Training Regulations/NC levels (links to W3811) and to BuildRight&#x27;s competency framework (links to VS-19.4/W683)
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / L&amp;D / Master Tradespersons
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3810_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3810_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3810_Task5" name="Trade Capability/Master-Tradespersons build the practical/on-the-job training…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trade Capability/Master-Tradespersons build the practical/on-the-job training design: store/DC rotation, fabrication-bay and estimation practice (links to VS-09.1/VS-09.2), shadowing, and competency sign-off standards, ensuring safety (links to VS-24) and product/brand knowledge (vendor content links to VS-01.3)
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / Store Ops / Master Tradespersons
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3810_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3810_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3810_Task6" name="Trade Capability/Compliance validate the curriculum against TESDA standards and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Trade Capability/Compliance validate the curriculum against TESDA standards and BuildRight policy, and define the assessment/certification criteria (links to W3819/W3811)
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / Compliance / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3810_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3810_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3810_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3810_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-598 (ensure controlled execution — Apprenticeship Program Design, TESDA Registration &amp; Governance (PA-123.1).) | - operational: master-tradesperson input; operational: TR mapping (links to W3811)
Owner: Trade Capability / L&amp;D</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
